<font face="Arial" size="+1"><B>Origin - CoNB Chat Log for 10/25/2000</B></font>
		<p></p>

<font face=arial size=-1><br><b>[Niobe]</b> Greetings and welcome to the Crossroads' third Roundtable Discussion between the gaming community and the developers of UWO:Origin. 
<br><b>[Niobe]</b> Tonight's question and answer session is an open topic discussion on the highly anticipated forthcoming game.
<br><b>[Niobe]</b> If you have a question you would like to have answered, please /msg Rico, Virgil, Aureus, or MadHatter with your question. 
<br><b>[Niobe]</b> Remember we may not be able to answer all of the questions submitted in the time allotted. 
<br><b>[MadHermit]</b> MadHermit not hatter
<br><b>[Niobe]</b> Please message only the above question takers. Do not message any members of the development team or your question will not be answered.
<br><b>[Niobe]</b> Oops!
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Please, no throwing of undergarments towards the dev team.
<br><b>[Niobe]</b> For unmoderated discussion during the chat, please join #ultima-online2
<br><b>[Niobe]</b> Thank you for coming tonight and we will begin accepting questions now!
<br><b>[Niobe]</b> And Cynthe has a few words to say while we get your questions
<br><b>[Cynthe]</b> Hey there!  Glad to see you all here... Ilove these full rooms. :)  There was a lot of interest lately in the reputation system, and Windfeather is on hand to answer some if he can... but his fingers can only type so much in a short time, and we have some of our great programmers here too to answer some of the more technical questions.  Plus, there's Ubiq, who handles all the flaming kitten questions. :)


<p><b>[Niobe]</b> *ImaFreak* Will you be including Words of Power? (i.e. Corp Por for EBolt) I think this was great, and since it was in the Uo2 Fiction, I am hoping you will include it.

<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Probably.  We like the words of power a lot.  Problem is - we have more spells.  That means that we have to be pretty creative 
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> I am going to change my legal name to Corp Por.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> coming up with Ultima-esque names.  Short of adding new syllables, it's a real challenge.  But it is something we hope to get to do.


<p><b>[Niobe]</b> *BaronGaran* I'm interested in the economy moreso than anything else... Is there going to be an unlimited amount of gold in the system like UO, or will it be limited, minted when it needs to be?

<br><b>[Mobius]</b> We'll have a theoretically unlimited gold supply. Why?...
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Russia should ask their central bank that about the Ruble.
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> Because if we have a limited supply, it'll eventually end up in the hands of a small...
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> percentage of the players.  They
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> They'll hoard it just because they can...
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> And that's just not a lot of fun...
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> The idea, however, is to have a lot of gold sinks to keep the gold inflation...
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> under wraps.  Players will also be able to barter in whatever they feel...
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> is valuable.  That's a good fall back in that bad case of gold becomming worthless.


<p><b>[Niobe]</b> *Ar-Kane* Is Necromancy one of the master school of magic? Aye or Nay

<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Maaaybe.
<br><b>[Cynthe]</b> sssh... it's a secret :)


<p><b>[Niobe]</b> *Frostburn* Approximately how many types of spell reagents will there be, if there are reagents?

<br><b>[Mobius]</b> Funny you should ask that...
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> I'm currently adding all of the reagent spawners to the game...
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> More than 20 at this point. It depends a lot on what exactly you consider a reagent...
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> some materials have more uses than just for spell casting.


<p><b>[Niobe]</b> *UrLord* how large is the flaming kitten juggling skill tree?

<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Well, it is definitely a pretty small tree, given that it is theoretical only.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> However, if we were to have flaming kittens, then that tree would be pretty big.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> poke


<p><b>[Niobe]</b> *ImaFreak* Do trade skills have sounds and actions? In UO, this was only to a certain degree, but EQ didn't have any at all!

<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Well...
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Yes, they do.  We can attach an animation and sound to just about any action.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> However, not everything will have one since some projects take time to complete.


<p><b>[Niobe]</b> *yude* will stealing from players be a viable profession?

<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> You can steal in Origin, but it's definitely not without consequences.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Our goal is to make the risk/reward for stealing commensurate with that for other risky activities...
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Plus, take into account the fact that your victims dislike being victims and need to be able to satisfy their desire for revenge.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> You won't be able to hang out at the bank and pester people all day.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> I should mention we have some other thief-type skills that are pretty exciting :)


<p><b>[Niobe]</b> *_Case_* We've seen moon&night screenshots...in UO the "In Lor" spell ruined it all...as there was in fact no night. I myself autobanned that spell...how will it be in Origin?

<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Due to our 3D engine, we can have more realistic and interesting light-type spells.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Even with our light spells active, you'll know it's night time.


<p><b>[Niobe]</b> *Vernes* Will werewolf deceases be in? Polymorph into a creature when the moon is full?

<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> But you will be able to see.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> That's not currently slated for the initial release of the game.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Perhaps if demand is high enough, a post-ship feature, but we're not looking at doing that feature right now.


<p><b>[Niobe]</b> *Jim_Dewit* when i cast a spell, or swing a sword, will the game engine require a target to be there, or can i do those things whether anyone is there or not?

<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Someone asked about that on the boards, so I checked it with Gaffer...yes, we can make a combat animation something you can 'show off' without requiring you to have a target.  Spells, possibly not, but can't say for sure.


<p><b>[Niobe]</b> *UrLord* can you guys tell us anything about mana? do you guys have a mana type system, or is it entirely reagent based?

<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Better.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> We are trying something new.  Each spell has it's own unique mana pool, which must recharge.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> I think it's the coolest magic system I have ever seen :)
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> This allows us to have more powerful spells, since we can give those spells slower recharge, and still ensure that lower level spells remain useful.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> So in one fair swoop, the system gives mages more powerful goodies, and yet improves the balance between mage and fighter.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Even a once a week, once a month, once a year spell.


<p><b>[Niobe]</b> *J23SE* can you elaborate on that 'other thief-type skills'? :)

<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Sure, you can do...
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> thief stuff.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Actually:
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> The one part I find the coolest is from our treasure system.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Monsters will have a chance to carry a portable chest.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> These chests will contain lots more treasure than normal...
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Locked, maybe trapped, etc.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> You'll need a rogue in your party if you want to get your loot.


<p><b>[Niobe]</b> *Icon|UH* Will the party system retain it's simplicity from Ultima Online, or will it have a new *technique*

<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> (They'll be common enough that having a rogue along will really help your hunting)
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Parties...
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> It's similar to EQ and UO - you get a roster of characters, but we have a wide range of ways to manage and track what your party has done.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> So it will feel much more like a team.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> It's simple yet complex!
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> 'Simple yet DEEP' ;)


<p><b>[Niobe]</b> *UrLord* can you tell us anything about the hybrid schools of magic?

<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Sure.  One of the schools is 'Nature', which is Earth + Water.  That is where the druid spells are found.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> We've tried to capture and place some 'logical' spell schools into that heirarchy, so that they are still achievable.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> The hybrid schools are designed to be difficult to get but still within the realm of a relatively casual gamer.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> It's like having a bag of jelly bellies and combining them into new and exciting flavors.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> I think it'll be cool.  If not, we'll tweak it til it is in beta. =)


<p><b>[Niobe]</b> *GiB_WaKeR* How close is Britian's layout in UOW:O compared to UO?  Or has it been completely chnaged due to the 3D Engine?

<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Well, cataclysms are kinda nasty
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Yeah, there's this big hole where - nevermind.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> They tend to do pretty wild stuff overall.  Some of the UO cities were lost in the apocalypse.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> On the other hand, the world is considerably larger.  It takes far longer to get from Britain to Yew than it used to.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> That's largely due to the appearance of distance in a 3D space.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> I think it's because the world is bloody huge.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> There are definitely changes, but overall, I think we've created a much more exciting and vibrant world.


<p><b>[Niobe]</b> *Ravodor* How is the particle effects system coming?

<br><b>[Hyperion]</b> Our tool is now online, and we've got an artist cranking away at creating new effects. The entire system is coming online now; just today I saw someone cast a spell and set someone on fire. Unfortunately, it was a healing spell.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Damn, PvP loopholes already.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> heheh


<p><b>[Niobe]</b> *Feynd* Will it be possible to become a high level warrior, then dislearn all your skills, and become a grandmaster craftsman?

<br><b>[Mobius]</b> In theory, yes. It would take a long time, however.


<p><b>[Niobe]</b> *Ender* In UO, it was possible to become the best in 7 skills only. How will UO2 regulate skill experience?

<br><b>[Mobius]</b> The way are skill trees are set up....
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> they are generally too big to be good at everything...
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> If you are a blacksmith, you'll probably have to specialize in single area or two...
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> Like sword smithing or axe smithing...
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> There's just too much to be an incredible blacksmith in everything.


<p><b>[Niobe]</b> *Frostburn* Will the entire skill tree be visible even if the player does not have the previous skills?

<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Given the vast enormity of our skill trees
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> That would be an incredibly daunting thing to see.  At launch we'll have WELL over 1000 skills, and that number is going to keep growing.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> As the game stays live.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> We're going to sell UO2 wallpaper on the site.  Paper your walls with the skill trees, only 49.95.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> So in order to keep things manageable for the newbie, we will focus the in-game experience on the skills immediately within their grasp.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> We will also work to provide information about the rest of the skill trees as well, and I'm sure the fan sites will help out. =)


<p><b>[Niobe]</b> *Vodka-7* To what extent will the LOD system be controllable by the end-user? For instance, can I force the game to always use the lowest quality models available (for max speed)? Can I force it to use the highest quality models (e.g., for taking the best screenshots)?

<br><b>[Hyperion]</b> The LOD system takes into account the current performance, the options setting, and the user's global setting. You should be able to crank up the global level to get more detailed models at the expense of a lower frame rate.
<br><b>[Hyperion]</b> However, the system will still adapt to the game environment as it changes. For example, if you wander in from a barren desert, expect the detail of models to be reduced as the system compensates for the increased geometry load.


<p><b>[Niobe]</b> *Keryath* when it comes to the Non-PVP zones, how will PvP attacks be handled? Is it going to be based upon the UO "insta-guards" or will it be like the EQ "smurf servers", where you simply can not affect the other players? If it's the latter, how do you decide what spells fuction and which don't?

<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> PvP in the safe lands will be 'EQ style' in that you simply cannot engage in such actions.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> This keeps in line with our fiction for the area...
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> And we'll simply have a bit to flip in each spell's database entry as to whether it's PvP or not.  Most of it won't require special code.


<p><b>[Niobe]</b> *Icon|UH* I watched one of the QuickTime movies, I noticed that a Juka did a "Misty Flip" over a human (Britannian)...Will this type of move be possible by a normal player character?

<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Will there be flying jump kicks and super triple flips?  Yes.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Will that specific move make it in?  Unsure.


<p><b>[Niobe]</b> *GTA* will the spells have animation such as color and swirling light and lots of effects...i didn't like the dull ones in uo where you casted it and you heard a noise and saw like 1 flash

<br><b>[Hyperion]</b> There are separate animations that we can combine to make spell casting more varied. Most of the magic schools have unique animation "wind-ups" that portray a gathering of energy. This can be combine with a unique particle system also related to the school.
<br><b>[Hyperion]</b> Then we follow that up with a unique 
<br><b>[Hyperion]</b> "delivery" animation, and the number of visual possibities *greatly* increases. The visual uniqueness of spells
<br><b>[Hyperion]</b> will have a fairly large variety. At the very least, you should be able to see someone beginning to cast a spell, and have
<br><b>[Hyperion]</b> some idea what school of magic they are using.


<p><b>[Niobe]</b> *Joshua_Rowan* How detailed will Titles be in Origin? Can you give some examples of what might impact a character's title, such as Reputation or Career Path?

<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> We have lots and lots and lots of titles.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Lots and lots and lots and lots
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> The format is similar to UO, in that (lots and lots)
<br><b>[Cynthe]</b> lots and lots
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Lots
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> there is a rep title before the name...
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Lots
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> (Crunch makes you delirious)
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> After your name comes your skill title.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> You will get a title for many of the skills you can learn.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> And then should be able to choose which one you display.


<p><b>[Niobe]</b> *Raven* How long would it take real time to walk your character from one side to the other of the largest and smallest continent?

<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> A freaking long time.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> lots and lots and lots of time.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Heh.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> I had to lay monster spawns for Britain last week.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> I felt like I was trying to paint the Great Wall of China.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> That also took lots and lots and lots of time.
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> Just wait until you do resource zones. :)
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Bah.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Anyway, probably two hours to cross Britain?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Seems low.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> A long time :)
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Britain the continent, not the city.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> That's britannia.


<p><b>[Niobe]</b> *GiB_WaKeR* Can you hint at any other "trivial"/social animations that will be available in UOW:O other than dancing, clapping, and waving hi/bye?

<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Yeah, that place.
<br><b>[Hyperion]</b> Okay, I'll let one more slip out. There is a bow animation.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Isn't there a barf animation?
<br><b>[Hyperion]</b> But it's different than the UO bow... ;-)
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Well, there are multiple bows.
<br><b>[Hyperion]</b> No, there are several vomit animations, though.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> I still prefer cartwheels.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> I wish I could have seen the motion capture for that.
<br><b>[Hyperion]</b> The vomit or the cartwheel?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> I wish I could have seen the motion capture for the spankings.  
<br><b>[Hyperion]</b> Everyone else did. It was a secret showing.


<p><b>[Niobe]</b> *CoNB_Guest1* Will is cost less to GM skills  such as parrying (or whatever branches are in it) then it would to GM sword fighting?  Who wants to be a grandmaster at using a Techno sheild and suck at swinging their sword?

<br><b>[Mobius]</b> The cost of mastering a given skill tree branch is relative to its overall "power"...
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> so yes, its cheaper to master shield use than it is polearms.


<p><b>[Niobe]</b> *Domnihate* How will the judician system work?  If I am arrested by town guards for theft will I have to spend (x time) sitting in a room (worthless), pay a fine, be banned from the city, etc?

<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Well...
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> We're still taking input on that, actually.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Most of the details on reputation I have posted have to do with tracking and identifying who has done something.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Some people want a prison, others fines, others beheadings.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Ubiq probably wants spankings.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Mommy?
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Anyway, we're listening to your ideas to see what we might go with :)


<p><b>[Niobe]</b> *Talebearer* What's the absolute worst thing a player can do to me if I leave the safe lands?

<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> That depends a lot on who you are, doesn't it?
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Use the vomit animation on you.
<br><b>[Cynthe]</b> Make you do the macarena.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Some people shrug off being PKed, but are strongly affected by sexual or racial ephithets
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Okay, I agree with Cynthe.
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> And some get the most angry at losing items to another.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> You CAN be killed in the wild lands, although murderers will have a very tough life it can happen
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> The idea is to make them a place where things can happen, but not a place where they always will happen when you go there.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> But I think we all know that the worst thing that can happen to you in an online environment isn't a death


<p><b>[Niobe]</b> *UrLord* how balanced are the types of weapons? for instance, will a longsword always be better than a broadsword, or will most weapons be viable as your main weapon?

<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Most weapons will be viable in different ways and to different people
<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> The only good way to design a game is to have a single best weapon.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Some are good vs different armors, some are easier to learn.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Some are better against mages, some are in skill trees that favor more useful critical hits.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> For example, hammers are more likely to stun your foe - if you have the skill to wield 'em correctly.


<p><b>[Niobe]</b> *J23SE* What presence will firearms have in UO2? I heard a mention of the blunderbuss. .

<br><b>[Mobius]</b> It depends on how you define firearms...
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> Our tech weapons are big and clunky, definately not modern...
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> They are powerful, but tend to be unreliable...
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> and even dangerous.
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> We've got blunderbusses, but we don't have any Steyr AUGs. :)


<p><b>[Niobe]</b> *Jenn_Reeves* Is there more heat seeking E-Bolts? The ones that would chase you as you ran around a  corner or is there a line of sight now?

<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Yes and no.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Some will chase you around corners and some won't.  Most effects travel quickly enough that you won't see many 'funnys'
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> But who says a fireball has to travel in a straight line.  WOuldn't it be more interesting if it curved gracefully?
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> However, i should point out that there's a reason why things clip through walls.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Remember, what you see in the client isn't what someone else sees on the other side of a phone connection.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> The time it takes to transmit the data means that sometimes you're going to fire something at someone in plain view
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> When on their screen, it looks like they are behind a house.
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> We've taken what actions we can to limit the number of things that look wierd, 
<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> but there will always be some, especially in cases of high latency.


<p><b>[Niobe]</b> *Bronwyn_Moonrose* will there be other types of missile weapons other than just bows and xbows? Like throwing axes, darts, slings, and the like?

<br><b>[Hyperion]</b> The client is always a "shadow" of what happens on the server, which is the "real" world. Sometimes the shadow may get a bit distorted, but its still a reflection of reality.
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> We've got some thrown weapons... plus we've got several different types of technological ranged...
<br><b>[Mobius]</b> So there should be plenty of variety to keep the ranged fighters happy.


<p><b>[Niobe]</b> *Gonj* Will NPC react to a Player's reprutation level? Say if the Dread Lord Roberts walks up to Joe the NPC blacksmith, will Joe refuse him

<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> That's certainly a possibility.  Right now the only definite plans are to have the guards hate you, so you cannot go into towns without being chased out.


<br><b>[Cynthe]</b> Well, the team has to get back behind their monitors, so thanks very much for taking some time with us!  We'll be around the boards when we can, and we look forward to hearing more from you. :)

<p><b>[Niobe]</b> Looks like we're out of time tonight.

<br><b>[Ubiq]</b> Sorry we're keeping it brief tonight.  The design team is cranking towards a major milestone, after which we will have lots of really cool stuff to show

<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Yeah, must lay monster spawns by Logos and Garron.

<br><b>[Windfeather]</b> Must...populate Bucs' Den...

<br><b>[Hyperion]</b> Thanks for all the questions. I hope to get to meet some of you at the UO Faire next month!



</font>

</td></tr></table>

